 ## Verified Facts
 
+- Store configuration `StoreView.usersContainers` explicitly uses `flex: 1 1 0`, an initial zero height, `min-height: 0`, and automatic overflow inside the existing bounded flex card. The list grows into the space remaining below its header and above its action, allowing excess user rows to scroll. Loading and user-card interactions remain unchanged; source review only, browser rendering remains unverified.
 - `CustAssetsAvatarUploader` accepts an optional `[MediaViewer.MediaFile]` image list, initializes the current avatar first, and shows at most four 12px selection dots beneath the preview. Selecting a dot changes the preview without changing the saved avatar; clicking the preview opens the existing MediaViewer at that image with media actions disabled. Asset-item detail supplies its existing photos. Upload results and external avatar changes restore focus to the current avatar. Reapplied on 2026-10-13 after accidental removal; source review only, browser/build behavior remains unverified.
 - `ManageLocationItem` exposes a bottom-left red crystal Eliminar action for an existing editor ID linked to a saved `.location` source. It uses the linked `locationId`, not the generated editor UUID, with the existing `deleteLocation` confirmation/error flow. The endpoint cancels the saved location without deleting its database record. Only success closes the editor and notifies `CreateTripView` through its existing saved-location list/selection cleanup; pending deletion prevents duplicate calls and saving. The existing `removeLocation` trip-stop operation is not called. Browser/server behavior remains unverified.
 - `CreateAssetItemView.create()` builds ordered image metadata from the existing upload registry, falling back to remote camera preview references by view ID. This includes uploaded camera files in `CreateAssetItemObject.images` while retaining the previous camera handlers, upload state and submission logic. Live browser/mobile behavior remains unverified.
